                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "36514305",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198037322518",
                            "num_reviews": 95,
                            "playtime_forever": 187,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 187,
                            "last_played": 1510333402
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I feel sorry for picking \"not recommended\".\nI mean this game is correctly finished and far from a tech demo or a crappy port. Graphics are good, UI is well thought, even the choice between virtual cursor and laser pointer is a great addition.\nThere are tons of different units, you must choose your unit set carefully or you will have a vulnerability (air, ground, repair, management, ....).\nCampaign is meh (no story, just doing maps with increasing difficulty to unlock stuff), but have enough content to be enjoyable. \n\nSo, why the downvote ?\n\nControls are a bit frustrating, as you absolutely cannot do any micro management. you just paint-select your group of units and give them a destination / target, and hope you have enough firepower to overpower the target location.\nYou can't assign a group of unit to a shortcut to micromanage your deployment, so faster units (usually the ones with less HP) will arrive first and get rekt before heavy tanking units arrive.\nNo micro management makes an assault just a swarm attack and let's hope for the best.\nThere's no strategy here, you don't plan an attack, you don't synchronize air troops with ground units, you can't separate things. It's more like a tower defense where you lead the swarm.\n\nIf that's your thing, then go ahead. If you want strategy, don't bother, you will end frustrated.",
